      ],
      "end": [
        580,
        330
      ],
      "greetings": [
        "The finches planted half that hedge. All I did was forget to close a sack.",
        "My sister used to cross that bridge barefoot, even in frost. I wear two pairs of socks.",
        "Let the pea vines catch your sleeve. Tender shoots hardly tug at all."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Oren",
      "role": "Bridge keeper",
      "start": [
        765,
        360
      ],
      "end": [
        800,
        391
      ],
      "greetings": [
        "Hear that? The creek pulls stones round all winter. By spring they're smooth as eggs.",
        "Stand still a moment. See that dimple behind the piling? That's where I'd cast.",
        "I left one plank creaky on purpose. The heron likes a little warning."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Mara",
      "role": "Cooper",
      "start": [
        267,
        318
      ],
      "end": [
        432,
        378
      ],
      "greetings": [
        "There\u2019s a sweet smell in a good barrel before you ever put cider in it.",
        "I saved the rings off your gran\u2019s rain barrel. They\u2019re still sound."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Tavi",
      "role": "Lamplighter",
      "start": [
        615,
        405
      ],
      "end": [
        697,
        319
      ],
      "greetings": [
        "The lamps at this end burn through their wicks twice as fast. River wind.",
        "I trim the wicks at noon so I can sit down for sunset."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Nell",
      "role": "Seed sorter",
      "start": [
        622,
        300
      ],
      "end": [
        565,
        368
      ],
      "greetings": [
        "Try holding those seeds in your palm. The full ones roll differently.",
        "The tiniest lettuce seeds make the widest mess on my kitchen table."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Ves",
      "role": "Potter",
      "start": [
        280,
        394
      ],
      "end": [
        396,
        335
      ],
      "greetings": [
        "Creek clay comes out blue until you fire it. Then it remembers the sun.",
        "I put a thumbprint under each cup. Handy when two families bring the same glaze."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Linn",
      "role": "Herbalist",
      "start": [
        817,
        305
      ],
      "end": [
        863,
        380
      ],
      "greetings": [
        "Rub one mint leaf between your fingers. Now smell your sleeve an hour later.",
        "Pick from three stems. A plant with half its leaves grows back sooner."
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "Pip",
      "role": "Post carrier",
      "start": [
        207,
        321
      ],
